{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_2>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        new Main().mainImpl();\n    }\n\n    private void mainImpl() {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int m = sc.nextInt();\n        sc.close();\n\n        Mod998 mod = new Mod998();\n        mod.init(n + m);\n\n        long phaseSize = 1;\n        long p = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; p != 0; i++) {\n            p = mod.mul(p, mod.mul(n - i, mod.inv(n + m - i)));\n            phaseSize = mod.add(phaseSize, p);\n        }\n\n        long ans = 0;\n        for (int k = 1; k <= n; k++) {\n            long numPhases = mod.mul(m + k, mod.inv(k));\n            long term = mod.mul(mod.ncr(n, k), mod.mul(numPhases, phaseSize));\n            ans = (k % 2 == 1) ? mod.add(ans, term) : mod.sub(ans, term);\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(ans);\n    }\n\n    static class Mod998 {\n        private static final long MOD = 998244353L;\n        private long[] fact, invFact;\n\n        public void init(int max) {\n            fact = new long[max + 1];\n            invFact = new long[max + 1];\n            fact[0] = 1;\n            for (int i = 1; i <= max; i++) fact[i] = mul(fact[i - 1], i);\n            invFact[max] = pow(fact[max], MOD - 2);\n            for (int i = max; i > 0; i--) invFact[i - 1] = mul(invFact[i], i);\n        }\n\n        public long ncr(int n, int r) {\n            if (r < 0 || r > n) return 0;\n            return mul(fact[n], mul(invFact[r], invFact[n - r]));\n        }\n\n        public long inv(int x) { return pow(x, MOD - 2); }\n\n        public long add(long a, long b) {\n            a %= MOD; b %= MOD;\n            long s = a + b;\n            return s >= MOD ? s - MOD : s;\n        }\n\n        public long sub(long a, long b) {\n            a %= MOD; b %= MOD;\n            long d = a - b;\n            return d < 0 ? d + MOD : d;\n        }\n\n        public long mul(long a, long b) {\n            return (a * b) % MOD;\n        }\n\n        private long pow(long base, long exp) {\n            long res = 1;\n            base %= MOD;\n            while (exp > 0) {\n                if ((exp & 1) == 1) res = mul(res, base);\n                base = mul(base, base);\n                exp >>= 1;\n            }\n            return res;\n        }\n    }\n}\n</your_rewritten_code_2>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\nusing namespace std;\n\nclass Mod998 {\nprivate:\n    static const long long MOD = 998244353LL;\n    vector<long long> fact, invFact;\n\npublic:\n    void init(int max) {\n        fact.resize(max + 1);\n        invFact.resize(max + 1);\n        fact[0] = 1;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= max; i++) {\n            fact[i] = mul(fact[i - 1], i);\n        }\n        invFact[max] = pow(fact[max], MOD - 2);\n        for (int i = max; i > 0; i--) {\n            invFact[i - 1] = mul(invFact[i], i);\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long ncr(int n, int r) {\n        if (r < 0 || r > n) return 0;\n        return mul(fact[n], mul(invFact[r], invFact[n - r]));\n    }\n\n    long long inv(int x) { \n        return pow(x, MOD - 2); \n    }\n\n    long long add(long long a, long long b) {\n        a %= MOD; \n        b %= MOD;\n        long long s = a + b;\n        return s >= MOD ? s - MOD : s;\n    }\n\n    long long sub(long long a, long long b) {\n        a %= MOD; \n        b %= MOD;\n        long long d = a - b;\n        return d < 0 ? d + MOD : d;\n    }\n\n    long long mul(long long a, long long b) {\n        return (a * b) % MOD;\n    }\n\nprivate:\n    long long pow(long long base, long long exp) {\n        long long res = 1;\n        base %= MOD;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) \n                res = mul(res, base);\n            base = mul(base, base);\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    int n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n\n    Mod998 mod;\n    mod.init(n + m);\n\n    long long phaseSize = 1;\n    long long p = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; p != 0; i++) {\n        p = mod.mul(p, mod.mul(n - i, mod.inv(n + m - i)));\n        phaseSize = mod.add(phaseSize, p);\n    }\n\n    long long ans = 0;\n    for (int k = 1; k <= n; k++) {\n        long long numPhases = mod.mul(m + k, mod.inv(k));\n        long long term = mod.mul(mod.ncr(n, k), mod.mul(numPhases, phaseSize));\n        ans = (k % 2 == 1) ? mod.add(ans, term) : mod.sub(ans, term);\n    }\n\n    cout << ans << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00012015574611723423, -3.933898824470816e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.0003469580551609397, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -6.198863957251888e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.001035987981595099, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -0.00016091958968900144, -0.0205434188246727, -0.005985194351524115, -1.7762025890988298e-05, -4.291525328881